-- title:
--   Primes over varpi at an end of the blow-up chart
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q\ge 5$, a non-zero natural number $M'$ with $q\nmid M'$, and a prime $\ell\ge 3$ with $\ell\ne q$ and $\ell\nmid M'$. Let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero, $\xi\in L$ a primitive $(q\ell)$-th root of unity (`hξ`), and assume `hι`: there is a ring homomorphism $\iota:L\to\mathbb C$ with $\iota\xi=\exp(2\pi i/(q\ell))$. Let $K$ be an intermediate field of $L\subseteq\operatorname{LaurentSeries} L$ which by `hK` equals [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103) applied to the $q$-expansion function field [`ModularCurve.xHFunctionField ((q*ℓ)^2*M') (ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH (q*ℓ) M')`](def/ModularCurve_XH.html#L79), i.e. the $L$-subfield of $\operatorname{LaurentSeries} L$ generated by the coefficientwise image of that field of $\mathbb Q$-rational $q$-expansions, the level subgroup being the kernel of $(\mathbb Z/(q\ell)^2M')^\times\to(\mathbb Z/ q\ell)^\times$.
--
--   Let $A$ be a Henselian discrete valuation ring with fraction field $L$ and algebraically closed residue field, with $q\in\mathfrak m_A$ (`hAq`) and $\xi$ in the image of $A$ (`hξA`), and let $K$ be an $A$-algebra compatibly with $L$. Let $j\in K$, non-zero, whose Laurent series is the image under [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb L`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81) of the $q$-expansion [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157) of the modular $j$-function (`hj`). Let $\varpi$ generate $\mathfrak m_A$ (`hϖ`) and let $\varpi_t\in A$ satisfy $\varpi_t^{\,q^2-1}=q\cdot u$ for some unit $u$ (`hϖt`). Write $C:=$ `chartAlgFin A ↥K j`, the $A$-subalgebra of $K$ of elements integral over $A[j]$.
--
--   Let $y$ be a maximal ideal of $C$ containing $\varpi$ (`hy`, `hϖy`) which is supersingular in the sense of `hss`: for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi:C\to\Omega$ with kernel $y$, the element $\varphi(j)$ lies in [`ModularCurve.ssJSet q Ω`](def/ModularCurve_SupersingularModuli.html#L7), the set of those $j$-invariants for which every elliptic curve over $\Omega$ with that invariant has no non-zero $q$-torsion point.
--
--   Throughout, a level automorphism at $\gamma^{-1}$ means an $L$-algebra automorphism $\tau$ of $K$ satisfying [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.IsLevelAutAt L (q*ℓ) ξ (q*ℓ) ((q*ℓ)^2*M') (ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH (q*ℓ) M') γ⁻¹ K τ`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelLevelAutAt.html#L29): for every weight $k$ and all modular forms $f,g$ of weight $k$ on the level group attached to $(q\ell)^2M'$ and `levelH (q*ℓ) M'` with integral $q$-expansions, $g$ with non-zero expansion, and every $x\in K$ whose Laurent series is the quotient of those expansions, the image of $\tau x$ under any $\iota$ with $\iota\xi=\exp(2\pi i/(q\ell))$ times the $q$-expansion of $g\mid_k$`conjElemN (q*ℓ) γ⁻¹` equals the $q$-expansion of $f\mid_k$`conjElemN (q*ℓ) γ⁻¹`.
--
--   The hypothesis `hArig` asserts a crossing presentation at every relevant point: for every point $z$ of the two-chart integral model $X:=$ [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel A ↥K j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236) such that the germ $\varpi_z$ of $\varpi$ at $z$ lies in $\mathfrak m_{\mathcal O_{X,z}}$, and every point $y'$ of $\operatorname{Spec} C$ mapping to $z$ whose ideal is supersingular in the above sense, there exist a complete discrete valuation ring $W$, a ring homomorphism $\sigma:A\to W$ with $\mathfrak m_W=(\sigma\varpi)$, power series $f,u,v\in W[[X_0,X_1]]$ with $u,v$ units and $f\equiv X_0X_1^q-X_0^qX_1$ modulo $(X_0,X_1)^{q+2}$, and a ring isomorphism $e$ from the $\mathfrak m$-adic completion of $\mathcal O_{X,z}$ onto $S:=W[[X_0,X_1]]/(\,\sigma(\varpi_t^{\,q+1})\,v-fu\,)$, subject to seven clauses (summarised here): $e$ carries the germ of $a\in A$ to the constant $\sigma a$; level automorphisms over $\Gamma_0(M')$ preserve $C$; those with $\gamma\in\Gamma(\ell)$ fix $y'$ pointwise modulo $y'$; each such automorphism fixing $y'$ modulo $y'$ induces $\theta\in\operatorname{Aut}(S)$ compatible with the germ map, fixing constants, with linear part a matrix $M$ congruent modulo $\mathfrak m_W$ to $c\gamma$ for some $c$ with $c^{q+1}\equiv 1$, where $c\equiv1$ if $\gamma\in\Gamma(\ell)$ and $c\not\equiv1$ if $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)$ and $\tau\ne\mathrm{id}$; primes of $S$ over $\sigma\varpi$ with tangent forms $a_iX_0+b_iX_1$ satisfying $q\nmid a_1b_2-a_2b_1$ have distinct contractions to $\mathcal O_{X,z}$; for a prime of $S$ over $\sigma\varpi$ with tangent form $X_0$, an element of $C$ lies in its contraction if and only if all its Laurent coefficients lie in $\mathfrak m_A$; and finally [`ModularCurve.jqNModC L (q*ℓ)`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L18), the expansion of $j$ in the parameter of level $q\ell$, lies in $K$ and in $C$, is congruent modulo $y'$ to some $a_0\in A$, and its difference from $a_0$ is carried by $e$ to a series $h\in(X_0,X_1)^{e_0}$, $e_0\ge1$, whose degree-$e_0$ leading form takes unit values at all pairs $(a,b)$ in $W$, not both in $\mathfrak m_W$, with $a^qb-ab^q\in\mathfrak m_W$.
--
--   Further data are fixed: a point $z$ of $X$ with $\varpi_z\in\mathfrak m_{\mathcal O_{X,z}}$ (`hϖz`, `hz`), a point $y'$ of $\operatorname{Spec} C$ over $z$ (`hy'`) which is supersingular (`hss'`) and satisfies $y'=y$ (`hy'y`), together with an explicit presentation $W_1,\sigma_1,f_1,u_1,v_1,e_1$ as above, the hypothesis `hW₁` being exactly the seven-clause conjunction just described for this data.
--
--   Let $J$ be the ideal of $C$ which by `hJ` is the infimum of all ideals of the form $r_\tau^{-1}\bigl((e_1\circ\mathrm{toC}\circ\mathrm{germY})^{-1}(\sigma_1\varpi_t,X_0,X_1)S\bigr)$, taken over $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$ and level automorphisms $\tau$ at $\gamma^{-1}$ preserving $C$, where $r_\tau$ is the induced endomorphism of $C$. Let $B$ be the $A$-subalgebra of $K$ which by `hB` is generated over $C$ by $\{x\in K:\exists i\in J,\ x\varpi_t=i\}$, that is the $\varpi_t$-chart of the blow-up of $J$. Let $\tilde W$ be a valuation subring of $K$ containing $B$ (`hBW`), and assume: `hR1`, that $C\subseteq B$ and $K$ is the fraction field of $B$; `hR2`, that $B$ is formally smooth and of finite presentation over $A$ and $B/\varpi B$ has Krull dimension at most $1$; `hR3` (five clauses), that an element of $L$ lies in $\tilde W$ exactly when it comes from $A$, that $\mathfrak m_{\tilde W}=(\varpi)$, that $\tilde W$ is a discrete valuation ring, that for $b\in C$ one has $b\in y$ if and only if $b\in\mathfrak m_{\tilde W}$, and that $\tilde W$ is the localisation of $B$ at the elements outside $\mathfrak m_{\tilde W}$; and `hEQ` (five clauses, summarised here), that for every $\mathbb F_{q^2}$-algebra structure on the residue field of $A$ there is a surjection $\rho$ from $B$ onto the Drinfeld coordinate ring [`DrinfeldCurve.CoordRing q (ResidueField A)`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L21) with kernel $\mathfrak m_{\tilde W}\cap B$, compatible with $A\to\operatorname{ResidueField} A$ and equivariant for level automorphisms over $\Gamma_0(M')$ preserving $\tilde W$ via an element $(\mathrm{redQ}\,q\,\gamma,c)$ of [`DrinfeldCurve.hSubgroup q`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L276) acting through [`DrinfeldCurve.hAction`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L325), with $c\ne1$ when $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)$ and $\tau\ne\mathrm{id}$; that level automorphisms over $\Gamma_0(M')$ preserve $B$; that every prime $Q$ of $B$ containing $\varpi$ contains $\tau(\mathfrak m_{\tilde W}\cap B)$ for some such $\tau$ with $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$; that an element of $B$ all of whose such translates lie in $\mathfrak m_{\tilde W}$ is divisible by $\varpi$ in $B$; and that a level automorphism over $\Gamma_0(M')$ preserving $y$ on $C$ preserves $\tilde W$.
--
--   Finally let $\mathcal O$ be a subring of $K$ satisfying `hO`: there are $a\in J$ with $a\ne0$ in $K$ and a maximal ideal $P$ of the $A$-subalgebra $B_a$ of $K$ generated over $C$ by $\{x\in K:\exists i\in J,\ xa=i\}$ such that $\mathcal O$ consists of the quotients $g/h$ with $g,h\in B_a$ and $h\notin P$, every element of $y$ lying in $\mathcal O$ is a non-unit of $\mathcal O$, and $B$ is not contained in $\mathcal O$.
--
--   The conclusion is twofold. First, $\mathcal O\subseteq\tilde W$. Second, there exist prime ideals $\mathfrak q_E\ne\mathfrak q_I$ of $\mathcal O$ such that: for every $f$ lying in both $\mathcal O$ and $\tilde W$, one has $f\in\mathfrak q_E$ if and only if $f\in\mathfrak m_{\tilde W}$ (so $\mathfrak q_E=\mathfrak m_{\tilde W}\cap\mathcal O$); if $\varpi\in\mathcal O$ then $\varpi\in\mathfrak q_I$; there is $b\in y\subseteq C$ such that, if $b$ lies in $\mathcal O$, then $b\notin\mathfrak q_I$; there is a non-unit of $\mathcal O$ outside $\mathfrak q_E$; there is a non-unit of $\mathcal O$ outside $\mathfrak q_I$ (so neither prime is the maximal ideal); and every prime $\mathfrak q$ of $\mathcal O$ which contains $\varpi$ whenever $\varpi\in\mathcal O$ and which is distinct from $\mathfrak q_E$ and $\mathfrak q_I$ contains every non-unit of $\mathcal O$, i.e. is the maximal ideal.
--
--   This is the local two-branch analysis at an "end" of the blown-up supersingular chart of the integral model: the primes of such a local ring $\mathcal O$ lying over the uniformiser $\varpi$ consist of the maximal ideal, the exceptional prime cut out by the valuation ring $\tilde W$, and exactly one further prime, reflecting the crossing presentation $\hat A[[U,V]]/(UV-\varpi^m)$ of the completion. It feeds the subsequent description of the fibre over the supersingular point and of the Igusa-type valuation rings attached to its branches.
